**Remember: Always reference this file for design decisions. Do not use generic or placeholder designs.**
 for bestpractices and # Unified Data & Context Layer

## Overview
Design and implement a unified data and context layer that normalizes integration data into canonical, tenant-scoped entities usable across dashboards, AI assistants, and workflows. This includes a generic UnifiedEntity wrapper, linking/sourcing metadata, versioning, soft-deletes, fast read endpoints, materialized views, and a robust linking engine to reconcile cross-system records. Enforce strict runtime safety checks (null/undefined guards) and dependency-first implementation order: auth/access control and core data setup must be completed before dashboard/workspace/analytics pages when both exist.

---

## Components to Build

1) Unified Data & Context Layer (Core)
- Purpose: Normalize data from all integrations into canonical entities: Company, Department, User, Contact, Lead, Account/Client, Opportunity/Deal, Project, Task, Document, KPI, Workflow, Activity, Alert, Conversation, Report, etc.
- Core Deliverables:
  - Canonical models with source pointers and reconciliation metadata
  - Ingest pipelines for structured and unstructured context
  - Linking engine to establish cross-system relationships (1-to-many, many-to-many)
  - Versioning, soft-deletes, audit trails
  - Tenant-scoped data isolation
  - Fast read endpoints and materialized views tailored for dashboards and AI
- Data Structures:
  - UnifiedEntity (Generic) wrapper
  - SourceReferences with provider, externalId, lastSeenAt
  - Fields: name/id, companyId (tenantId), entityType, payload (json), sourceReferences (array)
  - Relationships: belongs_to Company (tenant-scoped), and cross-entity links
- Storage:
  - Relational + JSON payloads, with materialized views for read-heavy dashboards
  - Soft-delete flag and version/versionHistory
- API surface:
  - Create/Update/Upsert canonical entities
  - Link/unlink relations
  - Query endpoints with tenant/department scoping and access control

2) Page: Global Dashboard
- Purpose: High-level landing dashboard showing aggregated KPIs, alerts, recent activity, and role-tailored quick actions.
- Deliverables:
  - Role-aware widgets, KPI tiles, activity streams, alerts panel
  - Data sourced exclusively from unified layer; include drill-down capabilities
  - Embedded AI-assisted insights strip (optional)
- UI Boundaries:
  - Global, multi-tenant scope; supports per-tenant configuration

3) Page: Single Department Workspace
- Purpose: Dedicated workspace for a selected department including overview, team activity, tasks/workflows, docs/resources, and department AI assistant.
- Deliverables:
  - Department-specific dashboard widgets
  - Team activity feed filtered by department
  - Department workflows and tasks with cross-system linking
  - Department docs/resources view
  - Department AI assistant pane with context from UnifiedData
- Navigation: Department-level routing and contextual sidebar

4) Page: Reports Center
- Purpose: Central hub to create, view, schedule, and export reports across tenants and departments
- Deliverables:
  - Report builder/templating system
  - Schedules, exports (CSV/PDF/JSON), AI-assisted summaries
  - Multi-tenant/department scoped report catalog
  - Access control and sharing options
- Data: Pulls from unified layer and materialized views

5) Page: Search Results Page
- Purpose: Global search across entities, documents, activities, and reports with filters and optional AI-assisted summarization
- Deliverables:
  - Global search input with faceted filters (type, source, department, owner, date)
  - AI-assisted summarization panel per result (optional)
  - Result ranking with role-based access checks
- Data: Unified layer + documents + activities + reports

6) Data Model: UnifiedEntity (Generic)
- Purpose: Generic wrapper for normalized entities (Contact, Lead, Deal, Project, Task) with source pointers
- Schema:
  - id (uuid) - primary key
  - companyId (tenantId) (uuid) - tenant scoping
  - entityType (string) - one of: Contact, Lead, Opportunity, Deal, Project, Task, Document, etc.
  - payload (json) - normalized fields (title, value, owner, status, dueDate, etc.)
  - sourceReferences (array<json>) - [{ provider, externalId, lastSeenAt }]
  - createdAt, updatedAt, version, isDeleted (soft delete)
  - linkedEntityIds (array<uuid>) - cross-system relationships
- Constraints:
  - All access/gating respects tenant scoping
  - Validation ensures payload contains essential keys per entityType
- Relationships:
  - Belongs to Company (tenant)
  - Many-to-many cross-entity links via linkedEntityIds

---

## Implementation Requirements

### Frontend
- Pages and routes:
  - /dashboard/global (Global Dashboard)
  - /department/:deptId (Single Department Workspace)
  - /reports (Reports Center)
  - /search (Search Results Page)
- Components:
  - UnifiedEntityCard, KPIBlock, ActivityStream, AlertPanel
  - DepartmentOverviewCard, TaskBoard, AIChatWidget (Department AI assistant)
  - ReportCard, SchedulePane, ExportButton
  - SearchBar, FilterChips, ResultList, AI_SummaryCard
- UI/UX:
  - Apply design system and color palette provided
  - Use 12-column responsive grid; hero-like hero sections only where appropriate
  - Guard all array operations: (items ?? []).map(...) and Array.isArray checks
  - Initialize state with proper defaults: useState<T[]>([]) for arrays; useState<UnifiedEntity[]>([]) for canonical lists
- Data handling:
  - Use nullish coalescing for all API results: data ?? []
  - Validate API shapes: const list = Array.isArray(response?.data) ? response.data : []
  - Optional chaining for nested objects: obj?.prop?.subprop
- Accessibility:
  - ARIA labels for interactive elements
  - Keyboard navigable widgets
- Performance:
  - Debounced search
  - Pagination/Infinite scroll for large result sets
  - Client-side memoization where appropriate

### Backend
- APIs:
  - UnifiedEntity endpoints:
    - POST /api/unified/entities upsert (upsert canonical entity)
    - GET /api/unified/entities?tenantId=&departmentId=&type=&search=
    - POST /api/unified/entities/:id/link (create cross-entity link)
    - POST /api/unified/entities/:id/softDelete
    - GET /api/unified/entities/materialized_view/:viewName
  - Ingestion endpoints for integrations:
    - POST /api/integrations/:provider/ingest
  - Reports:
    - CRUD for report templates
    - Schedule/export endpoints
- Database schema (high-level):
  - table unified_entities
    - id UUID PK
    - company_id UUID
    - entity_type VARCHAR
    - payload JSONB
    - is_deleted BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE
    - version INT DEFAULT 1
    - created_at TIMESTAMPTZ
    - updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ
  - table unified_sources
    - id UUID PK
    - unified_entity_id UUID FK
    - provider VARCHAR
    - external_id VARCHAR
    - last_seen_at TIMESTAMPTZ
  - table entity_links
    - id UUID PK
    - left_entity_id UUID FK
    - right_entity_id UUID FK
    - relation_type VARCHAR
    - created_at TIMESTAMPTZ
- Data integrity:
  - Validation of input shapes; enforce required fields per entityType
  - Versioning for all updates
  - Soft-delete semantics with audit trace
- Security:
  - Multi-tenant authorization checks
  - Role-based access: Admin, Executive, Manager, Member
  - Audit logs for data changes and AI actions
- Performance:
  - Materialized views for dashboards (e.g., latest KPI per tenant/department)
  - Indexes on tenant, entityType, and external source references

### Integration
- Ingestion pipeline:
  - Normalize incoming integrations to UnifiedEntity payloads
  - Preserve sourceReferences and external IDs
  - Run linking logic to establish cross-system relations
- Linking engine:
  - Heuristic and deterministic matching based on external IDs, email, names, and IDs
  - Conflict resolution policies and human-in-the-loop for high-value links
- AI context:
  - Ensure tenant isolation when retrieving context for AI prompts
  - Feed AI with structured payloads and links
- Data access:
  - Expose endpoints for read-heavy dashboards with pre-filtered materialized views
  - Cache frequently accessed reads per tenant

---

## User Experience Flow

1) Admin sets up tenant and authenticates
2) Admin connects integrations (CRM, docs, projects, etc.)
3) Unified data layer ingests, normalizes, and links records
4) User navigates to Global Dashboard
   - Sees aggregated KPIs, alerts, recent activity, quick actions
5) User selects a Department from the Departments area and opens Single Department Workspace
   - Overview shows department metrics, team activity
   - Tasks/workflows widget lists cross-system tasks with status
   - Documents/resources pane shows department-specific docs
   - AI assistant panel enables department-level prompts with relevant context
6) User opens Reports Center
   - Create new report templates, schedule exports
   - View/save/export reports by tenant/department
7) User uses Search Results Page
   - Enter query, apply filters, review results
   - AI-assisted summaries appear for relevant results
8) Across actions, all changes are versioned and auditable

---

## Build Order & Dependencies (Mandatory)

- Prerequisites:
  - Auth system with RBAC in place (Admin/Executive/Manager/Member)
  - Multi-tenant scaffolding with tenant isolation
  - Core API gateway and DB connectivity
  - Basic data ingestion pipeline skeleton
- Blocks:
  - Block 1: Core Unified Data Model + Ingestion endpoints
  - Block 2: Linking engine, versioning, soft deletes, and audit
  - Block 3: Materialized views and fast-read endpoints
  - Block 4: Global Dashboard UI connected to unified layer
  - Block 5: Department Workspace UI + AI assistant integration
  - Block 6: Reports Center UI + scheduling/export
  - Block 7: Search Results Page with AI-assisted summarization (optional)
- Sequencing Rule:
  - Auth/access control and core data setup must be completed before dashboard/workspace/analytics pages when both exist

---

## Technical Specifications

- Data Models
  - UnifiedEntity (Generic) with fields: id, companyId, entityType, payload, sourceReferences, linkedEntityIds, createdAt, updatedAt, version, isDeleted
  - SourceReference: provider, externalId, lastSeenAt
  - EntityLink: leftEntityId, rightEntityId, relationType, createdAt
  - UnifiedSource: provider, credentials, status, lastSync
- API Endpoints
  - POST /api/unified/entities/upsert
  - GET /api/unified/entities
  - POST /api/unified/entities/:id/link
  - POST /api/unified/entities/:id/softDelete
  - GET /api/unified/entities/materialized_view/:view
  - POST /api/integrations/:provider/ingest
  - Reports: CRUD templates, schedules, export
  - Search: GET /api/search with tenant/department filters
- Security
  - JWT/OAuth-based authentication
  - RBAC: Admin, Company Admin, Executive, Manager, Team Member, Viewer
  - Tenant isolation on all queries
  - Auditable actions for data changes and AI interactions
- Validation
  - Validate input shapes for each endpoint
  - Ensure payload conforms to required fields per entityType
  - Null/undefined guards for all array/object usages
  - Use data ?? [] for array results from integrations
- Runtime Safety (CRITICAL)
  - All array operations guard against null: (items ?? []).map(...) or Array.isArray(items) ? items.map(...) : []
  - Initialize React state with proper defaults: useState<T[]>([]) for lists
  - Supabase or API results: const results = data ?? [] and const list = Array.isArray(response?.data) ? response.data : []
  - Optional chaining and defaults in destructuring: const { items = [], count = 0 } = response ?? {}
  - Access nested API results with safe chaining
- Acceptance Criteria
  - UnifiedEntity upsert and linking work end-to-end with proper versioning
  - All dashboards and pages render data without runtime errors due to null/undefined
  - Access control enforces tenant and role restrictions
  - Materialized views provide sub-second reads for KPI widgets
  - AI assistant prompts respect tenant and role constraints and do not leak data

---

